# Healer CDA stack

Local-first Next.js planner: healer CD assignment → NSRT notes. No accounts, no WCL login, no backend.

## Stack

- **Next.js 16** App Router under `src/app/` (not root `app/`)
- **React 19** + **TypeScript** (`strict`) + path alias `@/*` → `src/*`
- **Tailwind CSS v4** via `@import "tailwindcss"` + `@tailwindcss/postcss`
- **Vitest** (node) for domain logic; ESLint = `eslint-config-next`

Read Next docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using APIs — this Next version differs from older training data.

## Layers (keep boundaries)

| Layer | Path | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| UI | `src/components/`, `src/app/` | Client UI, localStorage, presentation |
| Domain | `src/domain/` | Pure TS: assign, time, types — no React, no DOM |
| Data | `data/**/*.json` + `src/data/catalog.ts` | Boss/spell JSON; catalog only loads/types |
| Export | `src/export/` | Plan → text / NSRT strings |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — domain imports React or localStorage
// ✅ GOOD — autoAssign(boss, roster, tanks) stays pure; PlannerApp owns persistence
```

## Product constraints

- Healers: raid CDs, tank externals, raid-wide personal CD calls
- Prefer editing JSON timers / windows over new infra
- Prefer browser APIs + existing helpers over new dependencies
- Colocate tests next to domain: `*.test.ts`
